---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="The Crux Co builds a small number of guides, products and meals — each cut down to what actually works."
>
  <article class="container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <span class="meta-strip">About</span>
      <h1>Fewer things. Each one worth it.</h1>
      <p>
        The Crux Co is a small group of consumer brands built on one idea: decide what to leave out,
        then say so in public.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>We started with a news product</h2>
      <p>
        The idea was to cut fifty stories a day down to the ones that mattered — ten categories, five
        items each, under ten minutes. We published it every weekday from May to July 2026, and the
        <a href="/digest/">archive is still here</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        It failed as a business. Not because the writing was wrong, but because the model was: it was
        funded entirely by display advertising, which meant it needed a very large audience before it
        earned anything, and we never built one. Ad funding also pointed every editorial decision at
        traffic instead of usefulness, which is exactly the thing the product was supposed to be
        against.
      </p>
      <p>
        We stopped rather than keep publishing something that wasn't going to work. That's the least
        interesting part of the story and the part we're most willing to talk about.
      </p>

      <h2>What it taught us</h2>
      <p>
        The hard part was never finding things to include. It was having the discipline to leave
        things out, and the nerve to tell people what we'd cut. That turned out to be a more useful
        skill than a news product — so we pointed it at other things.
      </p>
      <p>
        Guides that end when the useful part ends. Products chosen because we couldn't find a better
        one, not because a supplier had stock. Food where you can read the whole label. Same method,
        different objects. <a href="/company/">Here's the full plan</a>, including the parts that
        don't exist yet.
      </p>

      <h2>How this one is funded</h2>
      <p>
        By people paying for things we made. There are no ad units on this site and there won't be.
        If we ever use an affiliate link, it will say so in the same sentence.
      </p>

      <h2>What we won't do</h2>
      <p>
        Manufactured urgency, fake scarcity, inflated prices with a line through them, sponsored
        placement, paid reviews, or any claim we can't show the working for. The full list is on
        <a href="/standards/">the standard</a>, along with the things that have already failed it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who writes it</h2>
      <p>
        One person, in India. Earlier essays were published under pen names; that was a mistake for a
        brand asking to be trusted, and we've stopped. If something here is wrong,
        <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> — corrections get published on the page where the mistake
        was, not quietly edited out.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
